{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"obi","ontology_prefix":"OBI","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0001751","ontology_name":"chmo","ontology_prefix":"CHMO","short_form":"CHMO_0001751","description":["A phosphate buffer, prepared from sodium phosphate, potassium phosphate and sodium chloride, where the pH is maintained by a phosphate–phosphoric acid equilibrium."],"label":"phosphate-buffered saline solution","obo_id":"CHMO:0001751","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["PBS buffer","PBS solution","PBS","phosphate buffered saline","phosphate-buffered saline (PBS) solution","phosphate-buffered salt solution"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/XCO_0000116","ontology_name":"xco","related_synonyms":["Krebs-Henseleit buffer perfusate","Krebs-Henseleit solution perfusate","Krebs-Ringer buffer perfusate","Krebs-Ringer solution perfusate"],"ontology_prefix":"XCO","short_form":"XCO_0000116","description":["A buffered, aqueous solution usually containing the cations sodium, potassium, calcium and magnesium, and anions chloride, sulfate, bicarbonate and phosphate and often including glucose as an energy source which is injected or pumped into, or poured through, an organ or tissue, usually via a blood vessel."],"label":"Kreb\u0027s solution perfusate","obo_id":"XCO:0000116","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/XCO_0000146","ontology_name":"xco","related_synonyms":["controlled oxygen content Krebs-Henseleit buffer perfusate","controlled oxygen content Krebs-Henseleit solution perfusate","controlled oxygen content Krebs-Ringer buffer perfusate","controlled oxygen content Krebs-Ringer solution perfusate"],"ontology_prefix":"XCO","short_form":"XCO_0000146","description":["A buffered, aqueous solution usually containing the cations sodium, potassium, calcium and magnesium, and anions chloride, sulfate, bicarbonate and phosphate and often including glucose as an energy source in which a specified amount of the tasteless, odorless, colorless gas essential for aerobic respiration with atomic number 8 has been dissolved, which is injected or pumped into, or poured through, an organ or tissue, usually via a blood vessel."],"label":"controlled oxygen content Kreb\u0027s solution perfusate","obo_id":"XCO:0000146","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MSIO_0000021","ontology_name":"msio","ontology_prefix":"MSIO","short_form":"MSIO_0000021","description":["Phosphated buffer saline (PBS) buffer is a buffer which is a water-based salt solution containing disodium hydrogen phosphate, sodium chloride and, in some formulations, potassium chloride and potassium dihydrogen phosphate."],"label":"PBS buffer","obo_id":"MSIO:0000021","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"micro","ontology_prefix":"MICRO","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"one","ontology_prefix":"ONE","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"vo","ontology_prefix":"VO","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63036","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"CHEBI_63036","description":["LanguaL term definition: Food additive; technological purpose(s): acidity regulator, buffer, emulsifier, humectant, moisture-retention agent, sequestrant, stabilizer, texturizing agent."],"label":"potassium dihydrogen phosphate","obo_id":"CHEBI:63036","type":"class"}],"numFound":9,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["XCO","2","FOODON","1","MICRO","1","MSIO","1","CHMO","1","ONE","1","VO","1","OBI","1"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","5","false","4"],"ontologyId":["xco","2","foodon","1","micro","1","msio","1","chmo","1","one","1","vo","1","obi","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/xco.owl","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/foodon.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MicrO.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/msio.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chmo.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ONE","1","http://purl.ob